\usage{
zanco_survival
}
\description{
Egg-to-adult viability (proportion of eggs eclosing to adulthood) for
\emph{Drosophila melanogaster}, measured per vial, across three
temperature regimes and two locally-adapted populations, on a geometric
array of protein:carbohydrate diets. Used in the package vignette
alongside \code{\link{zanco_wingsize}} as a worked, unpaired comparison
(viability is measured per vial; wing size is measured per individual
fly, so the two traits do not share a sampling unit).
}
\details{
The single constant-25 degree design point (a single design point with no
angular design, present in the raw data) has already been excluded, since
a quadratic surface cannot be fit to it.
}
